    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.animate\n\n### Description\n\nFirst of all: Thanks a lot for your work and time! :heart_eyes: \r\n\r\nWhen I use the `:terminal`, and output a lot lines, (eg when I build stuff) the `mini.animate` module introduces a very odd scroll behavior\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.0\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create the file `minimal.lua` with the content\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n-- Minimal config based on the example in folke/noice.nvim to prevent it from using existing lazy plugins\r\n-- https://github.com/folke/noice.nvim/wiki/Minimal-%60init.lua%60-to-Reproduce-an-Issue\r\nlocal root = vim.fn.fnamemodify(\"./nvim-repro\", \":p\")\r\n\r\n-- set stdpaths to use .repro\r\nfor _, name in ipairs({ \"config\", \"data\", \"state\", \"cache\" }) do\r\n\tvim.env[(\"XDG_%s_HOME\"):format(name:upper())] = root .. \"/\" .. name\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- bootstrap lazy\r\nlocal lazypath = root .. \"/plugins/lazy.nvim\"\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\r\n\tvim.fn.system({\r\n\t\t\"git\",\r\n\t\t\"clone\",\r\n\t\t\"--filter=blob:none\",\r\n\t\t\"--single-branch\",\r\n\t\t\"https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git\",\r\n\t\tlazypath,\r\n\t})\r\nend\r\nvim.opt.runtimepath:prepend(lazypath)\r\n\r\n-- install plugins\r\nlocal plugins = {\r\n\t\"echasnovski/mini.nvim\",\r\n\t-- pinning the commit to the one where I experienced the issue\r\n\tcommit = \"9f1f555\",\r\n\tconfig = function()\r\n\t\trequire(\"mini.animate\").setup({})\r\n\tend,\r\n}\r\nrequire(\"lazy\").setup(plugins, {\r\n\troot = root .. \"/plugins\",\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\n2. run `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n3. wait for the plugin installed\r\n4. restart `nvim`\r\n5. open a terminal with `:terminal`\r\n6. get into terminal mode using `i`\r\n7. emit some output eg using `cat`\r\n8. exit the terminal mode using `C-<Leader>C-n`\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nIt should just exit the terminal mode and NOT scroll at all.\r\n\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nInstead it jumps to, where the command started, and then scrolls (animation) back down\r\n\r\nVideo:\r\n\r\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/220049/235211031-0540ce8f-b3bd-494c-ad0d-e9b6c730e816.mp4\r\n\r\n",
